{% extends "base.html.jinja" %}
{% block title %}Adventure tutorial{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
<h1>Building an "anything goes" text adventure with LLMs</h1>

<p>This tutorial walks through a complete, working game: a single-player,
Dungeons &amp; Dragons style text adventure where <em>you can try anything</em>,
and a Large Language Model plays Dungeon Master. The twist is that the LLM
invents the world as you go &mdash; places, items, characters, lore &mdash; and
must <strong>save every invention</strong> through tools so the world stays
consistent turn after turn.</p>

<p>Every code snippet on these pages is read live from the game's source files,
so what you read is exactly what runs.</p>

<ol>
  {% for s, t in pages %}
  <li><a href="{{ link(s) }}">{{ t }}</a></li>
  {% endfor %}
</ol>

<p>Start with <a href="{{ link(pages[0][0]) }}">{{ pages[0][1] }}</a>.</p>
{% endblock %}
